        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): explain grayed-out rows in the new-session folder picker",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users browsing folders in the new-session picker would see grayed-out rows with no explanation. Disabled device rows (offline nodes or nodes without folder-browsing support), the admin-gated folder trigger, and dimmed dot-directories gave no hint why they looked inert, which reads as a bug (reported by a user on Discord for 7.1.beta5).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe picker already computed why a row is unusable (`connected`, `canBrowse`, `isAdmin`) but dropped the reason before render. Surfacing it as a native `title` tooltip matches the existing pattern in the same menu (the worktree row already explains itself via `newSession.worktreeUnavailable`).\n\n## User Impact\n\nHovering a grayed-out row in the new-session folder picker now explains it: \"Device is offline\", \"This device doesn't support folder browsing\", or \"Folder browsing needs an admin connection\". Dimmed dot-folders are labeled \"Hidden folder\".\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Extended `ui/src/e2e/new-session-page.e2e.test.ts` to assert the reason tooltips on the disabled offline/legacy node rows and no tooltip on the browsable one.\n- Codex autoreview clean on the branch diff.\n- i18n: new keys added to `en.ts` only; locale bundles are generated post-merge by `control-ui-locale-refresh`.\n",
        "branch": "claude/how-can-we-do-that-935972",
        "head_sha": "532d5436d4fbcd3a479bff22d0ac3c7a0185cc4f",
        "author": "steipete",
